  "page1": {
    "title": "Why Honesty Matters",
    "subtitle": "A small truth can keep a big friendship safe.",
    "body": "One day, Mina broke a cup at home. She was scared. She wanted to hide it.\n\nTelling the truth is hard. It also takes <u>courage</u>. But a lie can grow big and hurt people.\n\nMina went to her mom. She said, \"I broke the cup. I am sorry.\" Her mom was not angry; she smiled at her.\n\n\"Thank you for being honest,\" her mom said. \"Now I can <mark>trust you</mark> even more.\"\n\nMina felt light and free. A lie can hide for a short time, but the truth makes a strong heart.\n\nHonest people keep their friends, and people believe their words. Trust grows slowly, like a tall tree. So tell the truth, even when it is hard.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/mars/2026-07/04.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "Mina tells her mom the truth about the broken cup, and her mom smiles warmly."
  },
